// @error expected `}` to close the template hole but found NUMBER
// @error-at 7
// A hole holds exactly one EXPRESSION, and it has to end at the closing `}` —
// the only place the lexer mints a MID/TAIL part. Leftover input is reported
// here and then skipped to the next delimiter, so one bad hole does not swallow
// the rest of the file.
print(`${1 2}`)
